236ec5d654915b49e1c99ca89a3.001.1","identifier":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.23add83c8a842236ec5d654915b49e1c99ca89a3.001.1","sender":"w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov","sent":"2026-08-29T20:58:00-07:00"}],"sent":"2026-08-29T22:27:00-07:00","effective":"2026-08-29T22:27:00-07:00","onset":"2026-08-29T22:27:00-07:00","expires":"2026-08-30T00:45:00-07:00","ends":"2026-08-30T00:45:00-07:00","status":"Actual","messageType":"Update","category":"Met","severity":"Severe","certainty":"Likely","urgency":"Immediate","event":"Flash Flood Warning","sender":"w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov","senderName":"NWS Tucson AZ","headline":"Flash Flood Warning issued August 29 at 10:27PM MST until August 30 at 12:45AM MST by NWS Tucson AZ","description":"FFWTWC\n\nThe National Weather Service in Tucson has extended the\n\n* Flash Flood Warning for...\nWestern Graham County in southeastern Arizona...\nEast Central Pinal County in southeastern Arizona...\n\n* Until 1245 AM MST.\n\n* At 1027 PM MST, Doppler radar and automated rain gauges indicated\nthunderstorms produced heavy rain across the warned area. Between 1\nand 3 inches of rain have fallen in the Aravaipa Watershed.\nFlooding impacts will continue, but no additional rainfall is\nexpected. A stream gauge in the Aravaipa Canyon showed a rapid 6\nfoot rise and this flood wave is moving downstream. Hikers and\ncampers should move away from the creek now.\n\nHAZARD...Flash flooding caused by thunderstorms.\n\nSOURCE...Radar and automated gauges.\n\nIMPACT...Flash flooding of small creeks and streams, urban areas,\nhighways, streets and underpasses as well as other poor\ndrainage and low-lying areas.\n\n* Some locations that will experience flash flooding include...\nAravaipa Canyon Wilderness.\n\nThis includes the following streams and drainages...\nDeer Creek, Telegraph Wash and Aravaipa Creek.","instruction":"Be especially cautious at night when it is harder to recognize the\ndangers of flooding.\n\nRemain alert for flooding even in locations not receiving rain.\nWashes, streams, and rivers can become raging killer currents in a\nmatter of minutes, even from distant rainfall.\n\nFlooding is occurring or is imminent. It is important to know where\nyou are relative to streams, rivers, or creeks which can become\nkillers in heavy rains. Campers and hikers should avoid streams or\ncreeks.","response":"Avoid","note":null,"parameters":{"AWIPSidentifier":["FFWTWC"],"WMOidentifier":["WGUS55 KTWC 300527"],"flashFloodDetection":["RADAR AND GAUGE INDICATED"],"BLOCKCHANNEL":["EAS","NWEM","CMAS"],"EAS-ORG":["WXR"],"VTEC":["/O.EXT.KTWC.FF.W.0165.000000T0000Z-260830T0745Z/"],"eventEndingTime":["2026-08-30T00:45:00-07:00"]},"scope":"Public","code":"IPAWSv1.0","language":"en-US","web":"http://www.weather.gov","eventCode":{"SAME":["FFW"],"NationalWeatherService":["FFW"]}}},{"id":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.cc87ad84859e7c0138ed5c1afe63634605bac9bc.002.1","type":"Feature","geometry":{"type":"Polygon","coordinates":[[[-98.92,41.05],[-99.15,41.2],[-98.94,41.46],[-98.89,41.51],[-98.47,41.32],[-98.92,41.05]]]},"properties":{"@id":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.cc87ad84859e7c0138ed5c1afe63634605bac9bc.002.1","@type":"wx:Alert","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.cc87ad84859e7c0138ed5c1afe63634605bac9bc.002.1","areaDesc":"Greeley, NE; Howard, NE; Sherman, NE; Valley, NE","geocode":{"SAME":["031077","031093","031163","031175"],"UGC":["NEC077","NEC093","NEC163","NEC175"]},"affectedZones":["https://api.weather.gov/zones/county/NEC077","https://api.weather.gov/zones/county/NEC093","https://api.weather.gov/zones/county/NEC163","https://api.weather.gov/zones/county/NEC175"],"references":[{"@id":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.3b8453e952796ba985df8499433075c21a578b16.001.1","identifier":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.3b8453e952796ba985df8499433075c21a578b16.001.1","sender":"w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov","sent":"2026-08-30T01:51:00-05:00"}],"sent":"2026-08-30T02:07:00-05:00","effective":"2026-0